# Project Conventions

## Architecture

- **Cargo workspace** (`Cargo.toml`) with two crates: `crates/nexus-core` (engine + service layer, no UI) and `crates/nexus-gui` (native egui/eframe app, binary name `nexus`). No Node, no webview, no IPC.
- `nexus-core` has no UI dependency. One module per concern: `auth codegen collections console cookies docs environments fs graphql history http import mcp response runner scripts service types visualizer websocket`.
- `nexus_core::service::App` is the single entry point the GUI uses (sync CRUD plus async `http_send`, `runner_start`, `ws_*`, `graphql_*`, `mcp_*`; long operations take an event sink callback).
- `nexus-gui` layout: `app.rs` (NexusApp state + frame loop), `runtime.rs` (tokio runtime, `Msg` channel back to the UI thread), `state/` (plain structs per domain, persisted UI state in `~/.nexus/ui-state.json`), `panels/` (toolbar, sidebar, tab bar, request, response, console, runner, ws, graphql, mcp, `dialogs/`), `widgets/` (painted widgets, code editor, code view, a11y helpers), `editor/` (editor model + completion logic), `theme.rs` (dark/light palettes), `shortcuts.rs`, `dialog_ops.rs`, `payload.rs`, `highlight.rs`.

## Rust

- Errors: `thiserror` in core, `Result<T, String>` at the service boundary.
- Never block the UI thread: HTTP, scripts, runner, WS, GraphQL, MCP run on the tokio runtime (`runtime.rs`); results arrive as `Msg` and the handler calls `request_repaint`. File reads and heavy parsing go to `spawn_blocking`.
- All file writes and directory creation go through `nexus_core::fs` (0600 files, 0700 dirs).
- Before finishing: `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace`.
- Keep the dependency tree small; check `cargo tree` growth before adding a crate.

## Data Persistence

- Collections are directories under `~/.nexus/collections/` with `collection.json` metadata.
- Environments, history, tokens and `ui-state.json` are JSON/JSONL files under `~/.nexus/`.
- Item ordering is tracked via `itemOrder` arrays in metadata files.

## Naming

- Rust: `snake_case` files/functions, `PascalCase` types. Core tests live in `tests.rs` / `*_tests.rs` next to the module; GUI tests live in `crates/nexus-gui/tests/`.
